.Dd November 20, 2026
.Dt NQSMSIGN 3
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nqsmsign ,
.Nm nqsmvrfy ,
.Nm nqsmenc ,
.Nm nqsmdec
.Nd S/MIME: signed and encrypted mail
.Sh LIBRARY
libnoqtis, \-lnoqtis
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In noqtis.h
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmsign "nqsalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen" "const uint8_t *cert" "size_t certlen" "const char *entity" "size_t n" "int detached" "int64_t at" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmvrfy "const char *mime" "size_t n" "const uint8_t *const *anc" "const size_t *anclen" "size_t nanc" "int64_t at" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen" "nqx5f *signer"
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmenc "const uint8_t *const *rcert" "const size_t *rcertlen" "size_t nr" "const char *entity" "size_t n" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Ft int
.Fn nqsmdec "nqkalg alg" "const uint8_t *sk" "size_t sklen" "const uint8_t *cert" "size_t certlen" "const char *mime" "size_t n" "char *out" "size_t cap" "size_t *outlen"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
These functions are those of
.Xr nqcmssign 3
as mail (S/MIME, RFC 8551).
The content is a MIME entity: its header lines and its body, such as
.Ql Content-Type: text/plain ,
an empty line, and the text.
Its line ends are made CRLF before it is signed or encrypted, as S/MIME
requires.
.Pp
.Fn nqsmsign
signs the entity: an
.Ql application/pkcs7-mime
entity of the smime-type
.Ql signed-data
with the content inside or, when
.Fa detached
is not 0, a
.Ql multipart/signed
entity whose first part is the content in the clear and whose second is
the signature, so that a mail reader without S/MIME still shows the
text.
.Fn nqsmvrfy
checks either form as
.Fn nqcmsvrfy
does, and gives the signed entity.
.Pp
.Fn nqsmenc
encrypts the entity to ML-KEM certificates
.Po
.Ql application/pkcs7-mime ,
.Ql authEnveloped-data
.Pc ;
.Fn nqsmdec
opens it.
To sign and encrypt, sign first and encrypt the result.
.Pp
The results are text with CRLF line ends: the header fields
MIME-Version, Content-Type, Content-Transfer-Encoding and
Content-Disposition, an empty line, and base64.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
Those of
.Xr nqcmssign 3 ;
.Dv NQEDEC
also for an entity that is not of these types.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr noqtis-smime 1 ,
.Xr noqtis 3 ,
.Xr nqcmssign 3 ,
.Xr nqx5self 3
.Sh STANDARDS
RFC 8551.
